2. In this Notification —
“bank” means a bank that holds a bank licence under section 7 or 79 of the Banking Act 1970;
“finance company” means a finance company licensed under the Finance Companies Act 1967;
“merchant bank” means a merchant bank that, under the Banking Act 1970 —
(a)holds a merchant bank licence; or
(b)is treated as having been granted a merchant bank licence;
“qualifying payment” means any of the following which is deemed under section 12(6) of the Act to be derived from Singapore:
(a)any interest, commission, fee or other payment;
(b)any income derived from loans.
[S 330/2024 wef 15/04/2024]
